sum='Mario loved to have lots of friends and always showed off about how many friends he had at school. His grandfather bet him a fruit chaat that many of them were only companions or partners, not real friends. Mario accepted the bet but did not know how to test his friends, so Grandpa brought a “very special chair” from the attic – an invisible one. If Mario could sit on it at school, the magic would show him his real friends. At break time Mario asked everyone to form a circle and tried to sit on the invisible chair. He fell on his backside again and again, and his classmates laughed. Mario did not give up. Suddenly he did not fall – he was sitting in mid-air! Guneet, Asma and Deepa, three of his buddies, were holding him up, while many others only made fun of him. Mario understood his grandfather’s clever idea: true friends care for us; a friend never takes joy in our bad luck. That evening the four children visited Grandpa, who had won the bet, and enjoyed stories and fruit chaat. From then on they used the magic chair test, and whoever passed became friends for life.',
